Recommends: evolution-data-server
Description: Calendar application for Linux Mint Cinnamon (community fork)
 Mint Calendar (Community Edition) is a community-maintained, Linux
 Mint-flavored fork of GNOME Calendar, tracking upstream GNOME Calendar
 development and packaged independently for distribution outside the
 GNOME and Linux Mint release channels. By reusing the components which
 the GNOME desktop is built on, it integrates cleanly with Cinnamon on
 an Ubuntu base.
 .
 This build requires notably newer GTK4/libadwaita than Mint's own
 48.1+mint1 release did (GTK4 >= 4.21.2, libadwaita >= 1.8~alpha) —
 confirm your build environment actually has these before relying on
 this package; see the project README for details.
 .
 All credit for the underlying application goes to the GNOME Calendar
 authors and the Linux Mint team; this package is not affiliated with
 either project.
